{"key":"enterprise/T1021","id":"T1021","name":"Remote Services","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["lateral-movement"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows","IaaS","ESXi"],"environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may use Valid Accounts to log into a service that accepts remote connections, such as telnet, SSH, and VNC. The adversary may then perform actions as the logged-on user. In an enterprise environment, servers and workstations can be organized into domains. Domains provide centralized identity management, allowing users to login using one set of credentials across the entire network. If an adversary is able to obtain a set of valid…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1021","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--54a649ff-439a-41a4-9856-8d144a2551ba","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:48.472Z","source_object_version":"1.6","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0067","name":"Logon Session Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0067","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9ce98c86-8d30-4043-ba54-0784d478d0b5","page":"telemetry/DC0067/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0269","name":"Behavioral Detection Strategy for Remote Service Logins and Post-Access Activity","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0269","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--d33ffd4e-6328-4b10-84c0-7ad4a241b02d","relationship_id":"relationship--84cda73f-83eb-490a-a7ad-1b72f787ecd9"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0750","name":"Analytic 0750","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0269#AN0750","guidance":"Logon via RDP or WMI by a user account followed by uncommon command execution, file manipulation, or lateral network connections.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0269"},{"id":"AN0751","name":"Analytic 0751","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0269#AN0751","guidance":"SSH session from new source IP followed by interactive shell or privilege escalation (e.g., sudo, su) and outbound lateral connection.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0269"},{"id":"AN0752","name":"Analytic 0752","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0269#AN0752","guidance":"Remote login via ARD or SSH followed by screensharingd process activity or modification of TCC-protected files.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0269"},{"id":"AN0753","name":"Analytic 0753","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0269#AN0753","guidance":"Use of cloud-based bastion or VM console session followed by commands that initiate outbound SSH or RDP sessions from the cloud instance to other environments.","platforms":["IaaS"],"strategy_id":"DET0269"},{"id":"AN0754","name":"Analytic 0754","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0269#AN0754","guidance":"vSphere API logins (vimService) or SSH to ESXi host followed by unauthorized shell commands or lateral remote logins from the ESXi host.","platforms":["ESXi"],"strategy_id":"DET0269"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0067","component":"Logon Session Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4624, 4648","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0750","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0269#AN0750","validation":"upstream_defin